  "limits": [
    "60 MS/s has only +0.002 ns setup slack under the existing 100 MHz CPU clock and 0.300 ns input jitter. It is a constrained STA pass with very little additional margin, not a frequency-margin qualification.",
    "The four lower-rate images were built at a9a4ca9a. The 60 MS/s image is 0d67920c: only synthesis fanout and 60 MS/s physical-optimization settings differ; no address sequencing, numerical gate or cycle count changed.",
    "Two reset-fanout CDC-11 patterns, three Gray-bus warnings and inherited ADI CE/MUX handshakes remain visible. Protocol reasoning is in GLRT_CDC_REVIEW.md; analog metastability and external receive-eye measurements are not supplied by RTL tests.",
    "The inherited 13 RX data/frame and two ENSM external timing paths still require runtime interface calibration and PN/eye evidence.",
    "The new Linux device tree preserves Rev.C hardware identity and adds the GLRT marker. Earlier packages with the experimental model string are retained but are not these device-tool candidates.",
    "The existing rootfs is reused with only copied VERSIONS stamping; new kernel and device tree identify Linux 2ca294936430. No QSPI/bootloader/flash or hardware operation was performed.",
    "Candidate plans name an intended ad9361-1r1t runtime and exact expected model; they are not observations of current radio state and do not allocate a bench window.",
    "Hardware-owner messaging remains unavailable at the local MCP transport endpoint. Exact serial, current setup/image, rollback and an owner window must be established before any radio operation."
  ],
